# Without this, `docker build` sends the whole working tree as build context —
# including target/, which is 4.8 GB on a warm checkout. The build would appear
# to hang before it had compiled a line.
#
# Everything the artifact needs is here: the crates, schema/, corpus/, design/
# tokens, Cargo.toml and Cargo.lock. Nothing below is an input to it.

# Build output. The container builds its own from source; a host-built target/
# would also be for the wrong libc.
target/
out/

# Version control and CI.
.git/
.github/
.gitignore

# Agent and tool scratch. `.claude/` had reached 1.2 GB on this checkout and was
# being shipped as build context on every `docker build` -- found 2026-09-03
# while bringing up deploy/compose.yaml, where it turned a short build into
# minutes of context transfer before a line compiled. It is an input to nothing.
.claude/
.context/

# Documentation and review material — thousands of files, none of them compiled.
# `corpus/` is NOT here: it holds the statement dictionary the parser embeds.
docs/
*.md
!README.md

# Editor and OS noise.
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
.DS_Store

# Anything a previous run left behind.
*.log
scratch/
